{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people","id":1134808,"title":"Methods For Resurrecting People?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-28T05:39:54-07:00","id":1134808,"title":"Methods For Resurrecting People?","content":"Hello. I was wondering what ways are there for resurrecting people? Any power or ritual from any book will do, and the ones I'm trying to resurrect are mortals that have been dead for several (around 3) years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T07:12:24-07:00","id":1134825,"title":"","content":"There is a Relic available for the Aegis Kai Doru and a Benediction for the Malleus which can resurrect people, but I believe that they depend on how long the person has died, and 3 years may be a bit too much. High level Death Magic (combined with Life, perhaps) may work in case you are using Mage, but it may require Archmastery in order to work. Demons have an Exploit meant to bring dead people back to life, but again, it may depend on the time the person has died. Mummies may have something in their sleeve, either as a Relic, Seba or an Utterance, but I don't remember stumbling upon one even though it is appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T09:09:48-07:00","id":1134852,"title":"","content":"You can always use high enough Spirit of the particular concept - probably Rank 6+ Spirit of Healing could have 'Resurrection' ( fan made ) as his Numina. I use Rank 4 Spirits of Healing with Numina of 'Restoration' ( once again, fan made ) to let it heal &lt;It's Rank&gt; number of Aggravated damage to not let PCs die in games. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Those powers are fan-made, but totally in the cosmological rights of Shadow Realm ( and <b>Werewolf </b>). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T09:20:05-07:00","id":1134855,"title":"","content":"Changeling 1e had a powerful magic cauldern where you could resurrect someone by boiling them in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T10:02:44-07:00","id":1134861,"title":"","content":"There is a Resurrection Numina, but it is penalized by amount of days dead. Rank 6 and up things could break the barrier, though it would take a hefty price. LostLight mentioned the worm pipe but I think the time limit on that is a week.<br /> <br /> You're always available to plot devices. Powers like these tend to be better at them than just 'The Sixth Dot in Healing' ability. Research some obscure ritual, overcome the challenges to find it, gather the materials, make the sacrifice, they come back. You could add some extra problems on their part like they come back but want to burn everything, but after 3 years most people would have huge issues getting back into their life. Especially if their family, loved ones, and government thought they were dead already. Then you have things like paranormal investigators who would note that you're back and your grave has been dug up. Mages out to rip the secrets from your mind, Sin-Eaters attempting to put you down where you belong.<br /> <br /> If you have the opportunity you can always throw a curveball. 'They were never really dead!' kind of thing. Perhaps a True Fae kidnapped them and the dead ones are their fetches. Or they became vampires and faked their deaths. The God-Machine waves its mighty appendage and they are just alive again, destined for some purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-28-2017, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T10:26:37-07:00","id":1134868,"title":"","content":"Resurrecting someone is also the basis for many of the prometheans creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T10:32:29-07:00","id":1134871,"title":"","content":"How resurrected do you need them? I mean there are a good few ways to half-ass it if aren't too fussy.<br /> <br /> Like, a mage binding the ghost of a person to a construct that looks like their former body.<br /> <br /> A Promethean could use the bits of the mortal to create another Promethean. It'd probably look like the person and have some of their memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T11:04:49-07:00","id":1134881,"title":"","content":"There was a spirit of Resurrection in the back of Boston Unveiled, the Mage setting. It brought an almost random individual back from the dead but had to kill several other people first to power the Numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T12:51:46-07:00","id":1134905,"title":"","content":"The real problem is that they're fully dead, if they were only mostly dead we could work with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:03:33-07:00","id":1134940,"title":"","content":"We can at least look through their pockets for loose change.<br /> <br /> \u200bHowever you choose to do it just make sure there are issues, side effects and difficulties that have to be dealt with. Something that keeps it from being an easy method to cheat death while also providing interesting story, conflict and challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 08-28-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:21:44-07:00","id":1134946,"title":"","content":"Resurrecting someone is a Death 5 spell for mages, but the lucky Lazarus comes back soulless. Fortunately, any mage capable of bringing back the dead can fix that, given a suitable donor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:31:12-07:00","id":1134952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1134946#post1134946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resurrecting someone is a Death 5 spell for mages, but the lucky Lazarus comes back soulless. Fortunately, any mage capable of bringing back the dead can fix that, given a suitable donor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deny the Reaper requires a Potency for every month you want to 'de-age' a person. For +1 Reach you can 'return the recently dead to life.' Is it fair to use the same Potency requirement for the longer-dead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T16:02:31-07:00","id":1134980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1134952#post1134952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Deny the Reaper requires a Potency for every month you want to 'de-age' a person. For +1 Reach you can 'return the recently dead to life.' Is it fair to use the same Potency requirement for the longer-dead?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If a spell proves too difficult or impractical, you can always beg, barter or cajole a supernal entity for assistance who doesn't labor under the restrictions of normal mages.<br /> <br /> Never underestimate supernal summoning. However, I don't know whether even a Stygian summoned by a master of Death could resurrect some with an intact soul.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T19:42:01-07:00","id":1135032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1134861#post1134861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Resurrection Numina, but it is penalized by amount of days dead. Rank 6 and up things could break the barrier, though it would take a hefty price. LostLight mentioned the worm pipe but I think the time limit on that is a week.<br /> <br /> You're always available to plot devices. Powers like these tend to be better at them than just 'The Sixth Dot in Healing' ability. Research some obscure ritual, overcome the challenges to find it, gather the materials, make the sacrifice, they come back. You could add some extra problems on their part like they come back but want to burn everything, but after 3 years most people would have huge issues getting back into their life. Especially if their family, loved ones, and government thought they were dead already. Then you have things like paranormal investigators who would note that you're back and your grave has been dug up. Mages out to rip the secrets from your mind, Sin-Eaters attempting to put you down where you belong.<br /> <br /> If you have the opportunity you can always throw a curveball. 'They were never really dead!' kind of thing. Perhaps a True Fae kidnapped them and the dead ones are their fetches. Or they became vampires and faked their deaths. The God-Machine waves its mighty appendage and they are just alive again, destined for some purpose.</div> </div> </div> </div>The character being resurrected is based on L from Death Note, in other words almost completely anonymous and with very few people knowing his real name and face, so going along without being recognized wouldn't be a big issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T19:44:52-07:00","id":1135035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1134871#post1134871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How resurrected do you need them? I mean there are a good few ways to half-ass it if aren't too fussy.<br /> <br /> Like, a mage binding the ghost of a person to a construct that looks like their former body.<br /> <br /> A Promethean could use the bits of the mortal to create another Promethean. It'd probably look like the person and have some of their memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing that really matters is that the character has their memories and their mind intact, anything else is optional, and even the memories are not completely essential so long as he can still think and reason fine. He is being resurrected so that he can help solve some mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12947-enderdragon1201","name":"Enderdragon1201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12947_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T19:50:32-07:00","id":1135038,"title":"","content":"Ghost is enough, then. Given Materialize or a body to Possess/Claim and they are back in business.<br /> <br /> For bonus fun poking at the CofD ghostly condition... Have they themselves (or their source, rather) be responsible for a few of the crimes - having faked their own death, or been revived shortly after death. But their ghost doesn't know that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T15:40:01-07:00","id":1135284,"title":"","content":"Death Magic could turn the character into a zombie, maybe even able to access memories in the brain, and make sure the zombie stays in one piece. <br /> <br /> Time Arcana could allow a past version of the character to visit the present, maybe. <br /> <br /> You can have the character come back as a sin eater.<br /> <br /> Life arcana you can bring them back to life, abit soulless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T19:00:04-07:00","id":1135315,"title":"","content":"Worse comes to worst you don't have to explain it, just have it happen and leave it a mystery.<br /> They can learn about the attached baggage later, if an idea comes to you in play.<br /> \u200bYou never know, the player's guesses and wild speculation in character might give you the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T22:51:09-07:00","id":1135352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1134946#post1134946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resurrecting someone is a Death 5 spell for mages, but the lucky Lazarus comes back soulless. Fortunately, any mage capable of bringing back the dead can fix that, given a suitable donor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasnt there something about using Time to revers time until a time the corpse wasnt dead?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T01:04:16-07:00","id":1135365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1135352#post1135352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasnt there something about using Time to revers time until a time the corpse wasnt dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you go back in time and prevent the death, the person never died in the first place. This goes for preventing death that happened five years ago or one turn ago (saving a cabalmate by turning back time by a few seconds should be quite a common occurence for time mages).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T04:56:09-07:00","id":1135393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shaddar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1135352#post1135352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasnt there something about using Time to revers time until a time the corpse wasnt dead?</div> </div> </div> </div>You used to be able to resurrect people via Temporal Summoning, but that's no longer possible. There are other ways to do it via Time though (as Prometheus said)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T07:28:13-07:00","id":1135762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1134855#post1134855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling 1e had a powerful magic cauldern where you could resurrect someone by boiling them in it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting. In which book was this? I assume we're talking about the Cauldron of Annwn.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T08:43:12-07:00","id":1135788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1135762#post1135762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. In which book was this? I assume we're talking about the Cauldron of Annwn.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from Swords at Dawn, it's named the Cauldron of Rebirth, though it does hearken back to that time, also being called 'the Celtic grail.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T15:16:47-07:00","id":1135954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1134946#post1134946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resurrecting someone is a Death 5 spell for mages, but the lucky Lazarus comes back soulless. Fortunately, any mage capable of bringing back the dead can fix that, given a suitable donor.</div> </div> </div> </div> add to that a spell that stops your soul from leaving your body at death, like it turns you body into a soul jar, and you have that death problem licked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T17:14:51-07:00","id":1136003,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely sure that would work, since the soul doesn't really &quot;leave&quot; your body at death so much as it just sort of vanishes. <br /> <br /> You could totally get some other schmuck's soul and rig up a series of conditional hung death spells to resurrect you and stuff it in if you died though. Bit left-handed, obviously, but totally doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T18:15:31-07:00","id":1136027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1136003#post1136003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not entirely sure that would work, since the soul doesn't really &amp;quot;leave&amp;quot; your body at death so much as it just sort of vanishes. <br /> <br /> You could totally get some other schmuck's soul and rig up a series of conditional hung death spells to resurrect you and stuff it in if you died though. Bit left-handed, obviously, but totally doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Souls don't enable life, though. Nor even store one's consciousness. A body with a soul anchored to it is just a morbid soul jar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T18:37:19-07:00","id":1136036,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Methods of Resurrection </b><br /> <br /> While there seem to be a good number of canon ways to bring back the dead<b>,</b> I have always enjoyed home-brewing my own. Here is a relic I think might work for the use you have in mind. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Scroll of the Persephone </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span><br /> \u201cThe Scroll of Persephone\u201d is an ancient text written on papyrus with ink made from a blend of pyre-ash, blood, and pomegranate. The writing dates circa 300BC, in a dialect of Greek that would have been considered archaic even in that time. While faded and worn with age, the scroll has survived millennia and remains intact and legible. Its power is nothing short of miraculous \u2013 when the incantation is repeated properly, it can call back the dead. Those returned are physically, mentally and spiritually intact, but the magic fades overtime, with death reclaiming the returned after a short few months. The scroll currently resides under lock and key in a private collection of rare writings. The Scroll of Persephone grants its equipment bonus to Academics or Occult rolls involving Greek Mythology or Thanatology.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Equipment Bonus: </b>+2 <b>Size:</b> 1 <b>Durability:</b> 1(5) <b>Availability: </b>5<br /> <br /> <b>Powers</b><br /> The Scroll pf Persephone contains the following ritual, which can be performed by anyone with at least 3 dots of Academics or Occult. Performing these rituals is a Breaking Point with a -1 penalty.<br /> <b><i>Rite of the Black Pomegranate:</i></b> This ritual must be performed at night during the autumn or winter in a graveyard or similar place of death or mourning. It must be performed over the mostly intact remains of the deceased; the ritual does not work if the body has been reduced to ash and dust. The ritualist spends 5 points of Willpower and makes an extended Intelligence + Academics or Occult roll. The ritual requires 10 successes, with an additional success needed for every year the subject has been dead. Each roll requires 15 minutes of precise recitation of the verse and ritualized gestures.<br /> If successful, the subject is returned to life and health; fatal wounds are healed and fatal afflictions are cured. The ritual is ineffective on those who died or old age or similar natural causes or supernatural beings (including creatures that do not use Integrity to track Breaking Points). The revived person gains the <i>Resurrected</i> Condition and suffers a Breaking Point at a -3 penalty.<br /> <b><i>Indestructible:</i></b> The Scroll of Persephone is eternal \u2013 even if burned to ash or torn to shreds, it will re-appear in the nearest graveyard during the next new moon.<br /> <br /> <b>Drawback</b><br /> <b><i>One Foot in the Grave:</i></b> When the ritual is performed, the ritualist gains the <i>Open</i> Condition for Ghosts, which gain a +2 equipment bonus to use Influences and Numina against the ritualist. This Condition ends when the individual revived by the rite resolves the <i>Resurrected</i> Condition.</div></div> </div> </div></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T00:47:47-07:00","id":1136109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1136027#post1136027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Souls don't enable life, though. Nor even store one's consciousness. A body with a soul anchored to it is just a morbid soul jar.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, but I don't see what that has to do with anything I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T05:49:06-07:00","id":1136148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1136109#post1136109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is true, but I don't see what that has to do with anything I said.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right, my response was more toward <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a>'s point - your's just was the latest in that discussion and didn't directly address that issue.<br /> <br /> Though it does raise the question - if Ghosts behave (initially) as people who are soul-less (because they are, technically), would adding a soul to a Ghost make them even more like the person they came from? If you bind a soul to a person's Ghost, then have that Ghost Possess/Claim their old body, how different would they be from the original person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T06:16:02-07:00","id":1136154,"title":"","content":"The question you've gotta ask first is: Can you make a ghost actually use the soul the way a normal human can? It's certainly not as easy as making the ghost a soul jar because soul jars doesn't meaningfully use souls. They just house them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T06:37:50-07:00","id":1136164,"title":"","content":"The Post Moterm Embrace. Enough said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T10:29:55-07:00","id":1136244,"title":"","content":"Not enough said. Only works on fresh bodies. Absolutely not on someone who's been dead 3 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T14:39:51-07:00","id":1136378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134808-methods-for-resurrecting-people?p=1136244#post1136244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not enough said. Only works on fresh bodies. Absolutely not on someone who's been dead 3 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sense a nice reason for having Revenant-zombie then on the old bodies... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" 